From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:31:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 31/55] render: feed the engine uniforms Wallpaper Engine feeds

Decoded from wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485: the per-draw uniform switch
(GH 0x14010a0e0), the scene tick (GH 0x1401afbf0) and the time of day
(GH 0x14013f370).

g_Frametime (case 4): the frame's dt, renderTime - renderTimeLast, never
negative. It read 0, so cursorripple's step was 0.

g_PointerState (case 0x71): xy 1 while the left button is down, z 1 on
the frame it went down (WE's flags at ctx+0xa4: bit 0 down, bit 1 already
seen), w 0. From the host's wp_mouse_input is_pressed. It read 0.

g_Daytime (case 5) and engine.timeOfDay: the local time of day in
[0, 1), h/24 + m/1440 + s/86400 + ms/86400000, every frame from the wall
clock. Context::daytime was never written (0).

g_Time wraps every 432000 s (5 days), as WE resets its own (constant at
0x1404d44fc); scripts, particles and sounds keep the host clock.

Origin: ours
Why: g_Frametime, g_PointerState and g_Daytime/engine.timeOfDay read 0, g_Time never wrapped (docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B9: E4, E5, C1, C3, S18)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01288H8a42pVTGcB74tx4LjJ
